# =============================================================================
# E3-DoH Reproducibility — SHA-256 Manifest of expected_outputs/
# =============================================================================
#
# This file records the SHA-256 of every committed file in
# expected_outputs/. It is used by verification_script.py for the
# file-integrity check.
#
# The entries below are `<TO_BE_POPULATED>` until the first successful
# full-reproduction run. To populate:
#
#     python scripts/generate_manifest.py \
#         --outputs expected_outputs/ \
#         --manifest expected_outputs/MANIFEST.sha256
#
# That script is delivered later in the sequence. Until then, the
# verification_script.py reports "manifest SKIP" (not FAIL) because the
# entries are placeholders. This is documented in STATUS.md §9
# (ISSUE-01).
#
# Format (standard sha256sum):
#     <64-hex-digest>  <relative-path>
#
# A reviewer who has run the full reproduction should regenerate this
# file and commit it in the same commit as the expected_outputs/ JSON
# files. The file-integrity check is not a substitute for the
# value-based verification (the verification_script.py comparators);
# it is an additional check that the committed reference files have
# not been hand-edited after the sign-off.
#
# =============================================================================

